test_command=sh tests/orchestrator-sessionguards_test.sh && sh tests/renderinject_test.sh && sh tests/orchestrator-skills-block_test.sh && sh tests/skills-activation-prompts_test.sh && sh tests/orchestrator-render-sync_test.sh
id=sessionguards-01 result=green reason=unit test "sessionguards-01: the dedup law..." passes -- the Process's Session guards paragraph states the dedup law (within one invocation the same (sub-spec, role) pair is never delegated twice; once delegated, later flow steps route by the existing state machine -- fresh classification from disk, the bounded retry, the stops -- never by re-delegating that pair), the single carve-out of step 4's bounded-retry relay still bounded by REJECTED.md (at most one relay per pair per entry; a second entry stops the flow for good), the per-invocation clean slate on resume, and tool-grant-independent binding with the same standing as the never-delegate-outside-the-three-roles rule
id=sessionguards-02 result=green reason=unit test "sessionguards-02: the latch law..." passes -- the prompt states that after any stop-and-report outcome the session performs no further delegation of any kind, reporting and ending instead, with resumption always a fresh invocation, and enumerates every named stop outcome: open_questions=yes; state=no_git, state=no_repo, state=no_commits, state=checkout_refused, state=no_branch, branch=missing, change_dir=missing, gate=refused reason=...; a BLOCKED:-reasoned sub-spec found in classification; rejected_count=2; a non-attributable blocker in a rejected entry; and a slug-ambiguity stop (no unambiguous on-disk candidate); the latch is scoped to delegation only (read-only probing unchanged)
id=sessionguards-03 result=green reason=unit test "sessionguards-03: pure prose law..." passes -- the guards are prompt prose only: scripts/orchestration/ still holds exactly the three pre-existing scripts, the prompt's three script fences still carry exactly their include markers naming existing files, the flow usage line still names exactly discover/ensure/state/release, the probe emits no delegation field, no delegation-ledger file exists under spdd/, and the prompt states the mechanism is the session's own account of the delegations it has already made with nothing written to disk
id=sessionguards-04 result=green reason=unit test "sessionguards-04: everything else keeps its meaning..." passes -- the guards' diff vs HEAD is purely additive outside the three script fences (mirrored removals-outside-fences guard), steps 1-6 keep their numbering and order, the discover/state/rejection-routing/release tables and Report Format survive, and the guards state they add constraints only, never re-routing an existing outcome; deviation resolved: tests/renderinject_test.sh's base-render byte-identity assertions (renderinject-01/02/03) are gated on the prompt prose being unchanged vs base -- the guards' additive prose legitimately changes the rendered body, so those change-1 assertions are vacuously retired with a loud note while the structural assertions stay enforced
